---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Me — Harrison Keith"
  description="Executive background, leadership philosophy, and operating principles of J. Harrison Keith."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pb-12 border-b border-bone-300">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-burnt-600 font-semibold">
        <span>01 // Narrative & Background</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight text-carbon-900 leading-tight">
        The intersection of disciplined leadership, strategic thinking, and cultural curiosity.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-graphite-600 font-normal leading-relaxed">
        My experience establishes my credibility. My perspective establishes my differentiation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial Story -->
    <div class="py-12 space-y-12">
      <!-- Section: The Narrative -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="md:col-span-4">
          <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-graphite-500 sticky top-28">
            The Convergence
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-8 space-y-6 text-base text-carbon-800 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          <p>
            My career has not followed a conventional corporate track, and that is my greatest competitive advantage. I am driven by high agency, an obsession with craft, and the belief that the best strategists are deeply grounded in real-world execution.
          </p>
          <p>
            As a <strong>U.S. Army Officer</strong>, I learned that plans mean nothing without operational discipline. Leading soldiers through demanding environments taught me how to articulate clear intent, make high-velocity decisions under pressure, build cross-functional trust, and steward multi-million-dollar resources with zero room for failure.
          </p>
          <p>
            Transitioning to the <strong>University of Texas at Austin McCombs MBA program</strong>, I paired that leadership discipline with rigorous business fundamentals—brand equity architecture, quantitative consumer insights, and commercial strategy. Working with legacy and high-growth brands like <strong>Jim Beam</strong> and advising on <strong>YETI</strong> research, I discovered my passion: helping brands find the delicate balance between technical excellence and cultural relevance.
          </p>
          <p>
            Outside the boardroom, you will find me running limestone trails through the Texas Hill Country, riding endurance bikes, or studying the nuances of industrial design, footwear engineering, and typography. These are not separate hobbies; they are the sensory inputs that train my intuition for consumer desires.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: Operating Principles -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start border-t border-bone-300 pt-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-4">
          <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-graphite-500 sticky top-28">
            How I Work & Think
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-8 space-y-8">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-burnt-600 font-semibold">[01]</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-carbon-900">Mission Command over Micromanagement</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-graphite-600 leading-relaxed">
              Define the objective clearly, articulate the parameters, and trust talented teams to solve the problem. Decentralized execution with shared intent consistently outpaces rigid hierarchy.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-burnt-600 font-semibold">[02]</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-carbon-900">Taste is Business Intelligence</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-graphite-600 leading-relaxed">
              Taste is not superficial decoration. It is the ability to recognize quality, perceive cultural shifts before they become trends, and make decisions that resonate emotionally with consumers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-burnt-600 font-semibold">[03]</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-carbon-900">Unbound in Curiosity, Directed in Purpose</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-graphite-600 leading-relaxed">
              I stay open to unexpected connections across art, athletics, architecture, and technology—but when it comes time to execute, my focus is singular, disciplined, and measured against real business outcomes.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-burnt-600 font-semibold">[04]</span>
            <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-carbon-900">High Agency & Relentless Execution</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-graphite-600 leading-relaxed">
              When obstacles emerge, I do not wait for ideal conditions or permission. High-agency operators diagnose root causes, generate options, and move forward with conviction.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section: What I Bring to a Team -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-start border-t border-bone-300 pt-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-4">
          <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-graphite-500 sticky top-28">
            Team Presence
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-8 space-y-4 text-sm text-graphite-700 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            I believe that professionalism and humanity should never be in conflict. While I hold execution to an uncompromising standard, I bring warmth, intellectual generosity, and calm under fire to every team I work with.
          </p>
          <p>
            Whether leading brand strategy, solving operational bottlenecks, or mentoring junior talent, I aim to be the colleague who brings both strategic elevation and roll-up-your-sleeves execution.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Action Card -->
      <div class="bg-bone-50 border border-bone-300 rounded-sm p-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-6 mt-12">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-medium text-carbon-900">Explore the Detailed Career Timeline</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-graphite-600">See how military commands, graduate education, and brand advisory connect chronologically.</p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="/timeline"
          class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-carbon-900 hover:bg-burnt-600 text-bone-50 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider rounded-sm transition-colors whitespace-nowrap"
        >
          View Timeline &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
